Orvid bundles or builds on the following third-party work.

Java libraries (libs/)
- NewPipe Extractor 0.26.5 - GPL-3.0 - https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipeExtractor
- AndroidX Media3 1.11.1 (ExoPlayer) - Apache-2.0 - https://github.com/androidx/media
- AndroidX WebKit 1.17.1, Annotation, ExifInterface - Apache-2.0 - https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx
- Guava 33.3.1, failureaccess - Apache-2.0 - https://github.com/google/guava
- jsoup 1.22.2 - MIT - https://jsoup.org
- nanojson - MIT or Apache-2.0 - https://github.com/mmastrac/nanojson
- Rhino 1.8.1 - MPL-2.0 - https://github.com/mozilla/rhino
- protobuf-javalite 4.35.1 - BSD-3-Clause - https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf
- JSR 305 annotations 3.0.2 - Apache-2.0 - https://github.com/findbugsproject/findbugs

Native binaries (libs/native/)
- libtor.so from tor-android 0.4.9.14 (Tor, OpenSSL, libevent and their
  dependencies) - BSD-3-Clause and the licenses of the bundled projects -
  https://github.com/guardianproject/tor-android
- libgojni.so and libs/iptproxy-5.7.0.jar from IPtProxy 5.7.0 (Lyrebird obfs4
  and meek_lite, Snowflake client) - MIT, with BSD-2-Clause and BSD-3-Clause
  parts - https://github.com/tladesignz/IPtProxy

Data and assets
- res/raw/geoip_dach: subset of the Tor GeoIP file, generated from the IPFire
  Location database - CC BY-SA 4.0 - https://location.ipfire.org
- res/raw/bridges.json: default bridge lines from Tor Browser's pt_config.json -
  https://gitlab.torproject.org/tpo/applications/tor-browser-build
- Source icons from Simple Icons - CC0-1.0 - https://simpleicons.org
- Other source icons are the favicons of the respective sites. Names and logos
  belong to their owners and identify the source of a result.
